Tests that maxkins forward and inverse kinematics agree with each other.

The machine is driven to a series of poses with the pivot length, the tool
length and every one of B, C, U, V and W away from zero, and the position
that comes back through the forward kinematics is compared with the one that
was commanded.  A pose that survives the round trip is one where the two
directions of the transform describe the same machine.
